The proposed answer is incorrect. Jean II le Maingre "Boucicaut" was indeed a famous French commander present at Agincourt, but he was Marshal of France, not Constable, and he was captured at the battle (he had earlier been captured at Nicopolis) — he did not die there; he died in England around 1421.

The Constable of France in 1415 was Charles d'Albret. He held overall command of the French army at Agincourt and was killed in the battle, along with many other nobles (including the Duke of Alençon). So the question describes Charles d'Albret, not Boucicaut.

