The proposed answer is incorrect. The world premiere of Rachmaninoff's Piano Concerto No. 3 on 28 November 1909 in New York, with the New York Symphony Society, was conducted by Walter Damrosch. The confusion with Mahler arises because Rachmaninoff performed the concerto shortly afterward (January 1910) with the New York Philharmonic under Mahler's direction — a performance Mahler reportedly prepared with great care, rehearsing the orchestra thoroughly and respecting Rachmaninoff's wishes. But Mahler did not conduct the premiere itself.

The proposed answer's narrative actually inverts the facts: it was the later January 1910 performance that involved Mahler (with the Philharmonic), while the November 1909 premiere involved Damrosch (with the Symphony Society).

